  252                   
  253                   / Given a buffer of ascii digits, convert them to a binary number, return it in the AC.
  254                   / Base-10 is used.
  255                   / On call, the IO register contains the address of a buffer that contains one
  256                   / ascii character per word.
  257                   / Digits will be accumulated until a word of 0 is seen.
  258                   / If any character other than '0'-'9' is seen, processing stops
  259                   / and the number up to that point is returned.
  260                   / The IO register will have bit 0 set to 1 and the low 8 bits will have the character.
  261                   / The AC will have the number.
  262                   / No overflow condition is detected, high bits will shift out in this case.
  263                   / The maximum number is 98,304 unless AC is treated as unsigned, in which case it's 196,608.
  264 01073 000000      getnum, 0
  265 01074 241133           dac getnrt
  266 01075 341134           dzm getnbr
  267 01076 321135           dio getnbf
